# SUGGESTION: doc-comment misplacement — `_titleBar` lost its documentation

The new `_overflowStrip` method was inserted *between* `_titleBar`'s doc comment and `_titleBar` itself. The comment block now reads as one continuous doc for `_overflowStrip`:

```dart
  /// The title bar (issues #378+#457 AC2): the primary "open as app ...
  /// #457 AC2). The title tap still toggles collapse (#377 contract).
  /// The amber overflow strip (issue #692 C): the canvas reported content
  /// wider than the viewport; the agent got a one-shot note.
  Widget _overflowStrip(BuildContext context) { ... }

  Widget _titleBar(BuildContext context, ...) {   // ← now undocumented
```

`_titleBar` (the method the issues #378/#457/#377 text describes) is left with no doc, and `_overflowStrip` is documented with the title-bar contract. Move the overflow-strip comment (and the method) above the title-bar doc block.

Minor, same hunk: the strip is described as "amber" (here and in the l10n description) but renders with `colorScheme.errorContainer`/`error` (red family). Either use an amber tone or drop "amber" from the copy.

