{"content":"# SUGGESTION: silently swallowed overflow-note failure

```dart
}, onError: (Object _) {}),
```

If the `_sendText` back-channel rejects (session gone, agent mid-run), the overflow note vanishes with no trace — yet the one-shot `_overflowNoted` set has already consumed this widget's only report, so the agent is never told and the tile strip claims "The agent has been asked to rebuild it to fit." At minimum `AppLog.w('widgets', …)` the failure so the silent-degradation path is diagnosable; ideally don't mark the id as noted until the send succeeds (roll back `_overflowNoted.remove(definition.id)` in `onError`).
